            "bug_id": 19198,
            "text": "On Windows, Rprof()'s sampling thread (ProfileThread() in src/main/eval.c) resumes the main thread before writing each sample to R_ProfileOutfile. R_EndProfiling() only SetEvent()s the stop event and then immediately closes MainThread and fclose()s the output file, without joining the thread. A sample in flight is written through a FILE being closed, and the sampler's next WaitForSingleObject()/SuspendThread() use closed handles. Rprof(file) while profiling takes the same path and then replaces the global profiling state under the old sampler.\n\nTwo smaller issues in the same code: R_InitProfiling() passes the interval as a pointer to a stack-local `wait` and relies on Sleep(wait/2) for the thread to have copied it; and Rprof(NULL) with no profiler running still SetEvent()s and CloseHandle()s already-closed handles.\n\nI ran into this as a Windows CI failure on an unrelated change (https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/350): the process died in the Rprof() block of tests/reg-tests-2.R with no R-level error and no crash dump.\n\nBeing a race, there is no deterministic reproducer. The attached test in tests/reg-win.R restarts and stops the profiler repeatedly under load and checks that the earlier profile file is left untouched:\n\n    for (i in 1:5) {\n        Rprof(files[1L], memory.profiling = TRUE)\n        out <- lapply(1:10000, rnorm, n = 512)\n        Rprof(files[2L], memory.profiling = TRUE)  # restart while sampling\n        old <- readLines(files[1L])\n        out <- lapply(1:10000, rnorm, n = 512)\n        Rprof(NULL); Rprof(NULL)                   # second stop must be a no-op\n        stopifnot(identical(old, readLines(files[1L])))\n    }\n\nPatch attached as rprof-windows-thread-lifecycle.diff (against r90609):\n\n- _beginthreadex() instead of _beginthread(), so there is a joinable handle;\n- R_EndProfiling() signals, WaitForSingleObject(thread, INFINITE), then closes the thread, event and main-thread handles and the file, and only if a sampler exists;\n- the interval lives in a static that outlives the sampler; the Sleep() is gone;\n- the sampling loop continues only on WAIT_TIMEOUT;\n- DuplicateHandle() and CreateEvent() failures are checked.\n\nValidated on Windows x86_64 (Rtools45 GCC 14.2.0): 1,000 start/restart/stop cycles with a constant process handle count, 25 checks that an in-flight sample completes before its resources are released, and `make -f Makefile.win reg-tests-2.Rout reg-win.Rout` passing on a patched R, including 25 extra iterations of the existing Rprof() block. The new test also passes on macOS.\n\nAlso submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/356, where CI results can be seen.",
